for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DgQyPpFfgUN7wWKQgKicTd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
