{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EEgeAXiufXgh9b69xbgniu","type":"tool_result","content":"78:- 939 Actions; E.Action: action\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n957:- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1229:- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1236:- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1239:- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1244:- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773de6d-97d0-4491-ad74-18542d6086ce","uuid":"e588d361-77f9-45a1-86ac-47b4ceddbab2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:52:44.921Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"78:- 939 Actions; E.Action: action\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n957:- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action 