{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghztQA5fmUaSf4YWRVsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016GpkN8KVUPxLgDigk7pRTe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd .cache/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 1215,1260p API-INDEX.md; grep -n \"rig.update\\b\\|^- \\`rig\\.\\(update\\|draw\\|drawPortrait\\|solvePose\\|J\\b\\|C\\b\\|hand\\|kick\\)\\|new E.Humanoid\" API-INDEX.md | head -20","description":"Read arcade module index and Humanoid entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3049,"cache_read_input_tokens":188071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3049},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773de6d-97d0-4491-ad74-18542d6086ce","uuid":"f566d192-a2fa-4f1e-b191-eb63ff0f5f29","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:52:47.492Z","request_id":"req_011CghztPsj44GWBLNGAZcwq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016GpkN8KVUPxLgDigk7pRTe":{"command":"cd .cache/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 1215,1260p API-INDEX.md; grep -n \"rig.update\\b\\|^- \\`rig\\.\\(update\\|draw\\|drawPortrait\\|solvePose\\|J\\b\\|C\\b\\|hand\\|kick\\)\\|new E.Humanoid\" API-INDEX.md | head -20","description":"Read arcade module index and Humanoid entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016GpkN8KVUPxLgDigk7pRTe","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: line 1: cd: .cache/eng/dist/handoff: No such file or directory\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n668:- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\n670:- `rig.drawSmear(r, colors = ['#ffffff', '#dff8ff', '#8fe0f2', '#4bb1d4'])` †: motion smear for the current swing, queued in front of the rig\n671:- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n673:- `rig.kick(v)`: a squash-and-stretch kick: + stretches (a jump), - squashes (a landing, a hit)\n675:- `rig.solvePose()`: set the joints J from the rig's state this step (update and setPose call it); a clip player may wrap it on one rig: const base = rig.solvePose; rig.solvePose = function () { base.call(this); ...move J... }\n677:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }. spec.kick = true swings the right foot instead of the hand also aim (radians up), crouch, sprint, climb, hang (hangZ: the top it hangs from, above the feet), flip: 0..1 (a roll), pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' | 'die' | 'block', stance: 'guard' | 'ready', down: 0..1, vz (with climb: the climbing speed), land: k (a heavy landing), expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince', run: 0..1 (run in place)\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n680:- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n709:- `E.move(name, u = .5, phase = 'active')`: any move from E.MOVES at any moment, for previews and cutscenes: rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) (u 0..1 through phase)\n880:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders, knockback). const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22 }); update: hero.update(dt, level, game.input) (or an intent object for enemies: { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }) then read hero.onGround, hero.jumped, hero.landed, hero.facing (1 or -1), hero.climbing, hero.air draw a Humanoid with rig.update(dt, hero.rigState()) Units: world units per second. One tile = 16. A 285 jump with gravity 800 clears about 3 tiles.\n883:- `hero.rigState(extra)`: state for Humanoid.update: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack }))\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773de6d-97d0-4491-ad74-18542d6086ce","uuid":"b8a65a97-104c-463f-a2f6-086a2436ca6d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:52:47.541Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/bin/bash: line 1: cd: .cache/eng/dist/handoff: No such file or directory\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n668:- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: fa