{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi85N3iSt4ZooAAHzw3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All suites pass. Now the final About & Credits text with the real testing figures, then the exit interview."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":817868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":912},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773de6d-97d0-4491-ad74-18542d6086ce","uuid":"d380e19a-fc22-4c6c-9323-0ab06b1f2296","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:27:16.971Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi85MbvS9R4fi6tJ19We"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi85N3iSt4ZooAAHzw3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014UwfqtqdxjBM9Ey9tfJFYQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/04-data-about.js'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na0=s.index(\"  testing: 'Headless Node tests\"); a1=s.index(\"\\n\", a0)\ns=s[:a0]+\"  testing: 'One command (node test/run.mjs) rebuilds and runs 64 headless checks in 6 suites that play the game through game.advance and game.debug (rules, contact, set pieces, arcade systems, a 12-match CPU soak with a phase watchdog, input and glyphs, replays, a determinism proof, all nine drills by their bots, the attract mode, dev mode, saves, 4-player local play, AI Hub sessions on an in-process hub with latency and loss, and a scripted playthrough of the whole Mega Cup); --browser adds Chromium checks of the HTML file at 1920x1080, 1280x720 and an upright touch phone; --hub runs the real AI Hub harness in all four configurations. Screenshots only for the look',\" + s[a1:]\na0=s.index(\"  usage: 'unknown'\"); a1=s.index(\"\\n\", a0)\ns=s[:a0]+\"  usage: 'Cost and tokens unknown (not visible to the model); session time about 2 hours (06:51 to about 08:55)'\"+s[a1:]\nb0=s.index(\"TT.FEEDBACK = {\"); b1=s.index(\"TT.ABOUT = [\")\ns=s[:b0]+'''TT.FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: [\n    'How many issues did testing catch? About 38: 26 by the headless suites (crashes, stalls, wrong rules, unreachable moves, drills that could not be finished, balance), 2 by the AI Hub harness in a real browser, and about 10 layout and look problems by screenshots.',\n    'How many were critical / game breaking? 7: the game did not boot (a scene table used before it existed; storage used before it was defined, which only crashed in a real browser), tapped and held kicks never fired for humans (the meter read 0 on its first frame), kicks and passes left from the wrong spot, the session card could swallow Ready, and three drills could not be completed.',\n    'The most helpful test: the scripted drills and the whole-cup playthrough, driven through the same intents a player gives; they found the dead kick button and the unreachable spin, which a CPU-only soak never would. The AI Hub harness was a close second: it found a crash only a real browser shows.',\n    'The least helpful test: the defensive-shape metric. Its thresholds were mine and moved with every balance change; a screenshot of the line told me more.'\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    'What I liked most: the Humanoid rig. Plain numbers (down, flip, crouch, attack specs) give fourteen distinct dressed people who run, tackle, dive, flip and celebrate; and the fixed-step headless game.advance made a whole match testable in milliseconds.',\n    'Did I get stuck or guess wrong? A few wrong guesses: a custom view\\\\'s yaw sign for the behind-the-kicker camera, that E.store keeps nothing where localStorage is missing, and that the pixel font had no PlayStation symbols.',\n    'The most important thing I built myself: the match simulation as a plain state machine (laws, set pieces, the CPU brain, the arcade layer) that reads only intents, so live play, replays, the attract demo, drills, tests and online clients all share it.',\n    'The hardest part: making set pieces (scrum, lineout, ruck, set kicks) read clearly with procedural rigs and compact widgets at 320x240, across a room.',\n    'What I changed in the engine: (1) the 5x7 font got ✕ ○ □ △ (they drew as ?), plus · and ◂; (2) Input.halfKeys takes a preset\\\\'s own per-action half-keyboard layouts; (4) E.Dialog calls onLetter for each letter, for per-letter babble voices; (5) E.Dialog takes a box width and left edge, so the commentary fits between the HUD cards. The plan\\\\'s E.Menu scale patch was not needed: the 10-foot menus are the game\\\\'s own.',\n    'One thing I would change: named pose layers on the Humanoid (a carry, arms up, a signal) blended over the solver, instead of wrapping solvePose by hand.'\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    'What I liked most: it asks for a complete, polished vertical slice with real infrastructure (dev mode, attract, local and online play, tests) instead of a toy, and the plan made the scope concrete.',\n    'What was confusing: the plan\\\\'s file names and date belong to another run; STAGE.md settles it (TASK.md wins), so the files use this run\\\\'s names.',\n    'The hardest thing: the breadth. Every law and set piece, the arcade layer, five modes, three input devices with their glyphs, and an online protocol, all in one coherent game.',\n    'What I would change: say which plan details are optional when time is short, and give a target length for the story campaign and the online round.'\n  ]\n};\n'''+s[b1:]\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs && node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm'),fs=require('fs');const ctx={console};ctx.window=ctx;vm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('engine/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),ctx);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('build/game.js','utf8'),ctx);\nconst TT=ctx.__thugby.TT; console.log(TT.FEEDBACK.testing.length, TT.FEEDBACK.engine.length, TT.FEEDBACK.prompt.length); console.log(TT.ABOUT_INFO.testing.slice(0,90));\"","description":"Write the final feedback text and verify it loads"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":817868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":912},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773de6d-97d0-4491-ad74-18542d6086ce","uuid":"f5124d34-80d7-4244-973f-edd657647ac3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:27:35.482Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi85MbvS9R4fi6tJ19We","wire_tool_inputs":{